  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1056 PM CDT SAT SEP 12 2026\n\nA few showers will linger over the next few hours before clearing\nas the trough exits the region. Meanwhile, upper-level ridging\nwill quickly build in by Sunday, returning rain chances to a low-\nend, widely isolated, diurnally driven pattern. Latest CAMs show\nminimal rain chances in the far south on Sunday afternoon (15 to\n20%), warranting a slight upward adjustment in PoPs.\n\nDry conditions will generally prevail on Monday, though a stray\nshower remains possible in the far northeast during peak heating.\nConfidence remains low regarding overall coverage, so PoPs will\nbe kept at 10% for Monday afternoon as highs reach the mid to\nupper 90s. As the ridge continues to build through next week,\nrain chances will remain low (10 to 20%), with afternoon highs\nquickly rebounding into the low to mid-90s.\n\n16",
